    "updated_at": "2026-05-12T04:05:11Z",
    "body": "> you can use https://github.com/HolyRoses/tracker_query to examine your tracker.\n\nfrom what im seeing-\nwith a little test torrent between 2 clients-\nthe peer/seed count isnt incrementing each reconnect-\ni do believe a large reason why it kept creeping up was due to you using a different port each time-\nwhich is intentional by design as multiple people may be under the same IP due to ISP GCNAT and other trickeries as currently all ipv4 addresses are in use around the world- or well- theirs more people than ipv4 addresses",
