    "body": "> > you can use https://github.com/HolyRoses/tracker_query to examine your tracker.\n> \n> from what im seeing- with a little test torrent between 2 clients- the peer/seed count isnt incrementing each reconnect- i do believe a large reason why it kept creeping up was due to you using a different port each time- which is intentional by design as multiple people may be under the same IP due to ISP GCNAT and other trickeries as currently all ipv4 addresses are in use around the world- or well- theirs more people than ipv4 addresses\n\nand-\nthe rate limiting-\nisnt their lol-\nIt just happens naturally from it being made in python lmao\n\nanother note-\nSUPRISINGLY GOOD-\nfor 180 lines of code-\nIN PYTHON-\nlike- normally id expect something like this to be like 300 lines at least",
